{
  "id": "COMPOUND:14572 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that physostigmine may interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through multiple pathways. The drug is linked to LoVo cells, which are targeted by both 3-Hydroxy-7A-Methyl-1Ah-Naphtho[2,3-B]Oxirene-2,7-Dione and Furanocembranoid 2, both of which have the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex as their target. Additionally, physostigmine is associated with cortisol, which also targets the same complex. This indicates that physostigmine may exert its effects through different molecular mechanisms that ultimately converge on the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The evidence suggests a potential role for physostigmine in modulating the activity of this chromatin modifier complex, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated. The scores across all paths are consistent, suggesting a plausible relationship, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
